this paper, we first propose a structured framework tailored for LLM-based AI Agents and discuss the crucial capabilities necessary for tackling intricate problems. Within this framework, we design two distinct types of agents (i.e., one-step agent and sequential agent) to execute the inference process. Subsequently, we instantiate the framework using various LLMs and evaluate their Task Planning and Tool Usage (TPTU) abilities on typical tasks. By highlighting key findings and challenges, our goal is to provide a helpful resource for researchers and practitioners to leverage the power of LLMs in their AI applications. Our study emphasizes the substantial potential of these models, while also identifying areas that need more investigation and improvement.", "descriptionType": "Abstract"}, {"description": "Accepted in NeurIPS-2023 Workshop on Foundation Models for Decision Making", "descriptionType": "Other"}], "geoLocations": [], "fundingReferences": [], "xml": "", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.03427", "contentUrl": null, "metadataVersion": 3, "schemaVersion": "http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4", "source": "mds", "isActive": true, "state": "findable", "reason": null, "viewCount": 0, "viewsOverTime": [], "downloadCount": 0, "downloadsOverTime": [], "referenceCount": 0, "citationCount": 0, "citationsOverTime": [], "partCount": 0, "partOfCount": 0, "versionCount": 0, "versionOfCount": 0, "created": "2023-08-08T02:02:01.000Z", "registered": "2023-08-08T02:02:02.000Z", "published": "2023", "updated": "2025-12-30T03:42:38.000Z"}, "relationships": {"client": {"data": {"id": "arxiv.content", "type": "clients"}}, "provider": {"data": {"id": "arxiv", "type": "providers"}}, "media": {"data": {"id": "10.48550/arxiv.2308.03427", "type": "media"}}, "references": {"data": []}, "citations": {"data": []}, "parts": {"data": []}, "partOf": {"data": []}, "versions": {"data": []}, "versionOf": {"data": []}}}}